{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486804-blood-magic-at-this-point-is-extremely-common","id":1486804,"title":"Blood Magic at this point is extremely common","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-07-17T16:20:46-07:00","id":1486804,"title":"Blood Magic at this point is extremely common","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It seems almost every clan/obscure bloodline has Blood Magic at this point, and I think thats pretty cool.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">1) 4 different types of Setite Sorcery practiced by 4 different FoS bloodlines, with the most common being Akhu, and another lesser known type known as Nahuallotl which is most likely practiced exclusively by the Tlacique.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">2) Koldunic Sorcery practiced by the Kolduns of Old Clan Tzimisce.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">3) Assamite Sorcery/Dur-An-Ki practiced by the Assamite Sorcerer Caste, and a few Metheleusas. Becomes an in clan discipline for the Assamites in V5</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">4) Sadhana practiced by the Indian Venture bloodline known as Danava, Daitya (FoS Bloodline), a few Indian vampires that come from other clans, and the Trimira (Indian Tremere) which accept other vampires from different clans.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">5) Different types of necromancy practiced by the Giovanni, Samedi, Nagraja, some Haitian Lassombra, and some Serpents of Light. Replace by Oblivion for the Hecate in V5.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">6) Abyss Mysticism practiced by the mystics of clan Lassombra.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">7) Thaumaturgy and Selinic Thaumaturgy practiced by the Tremere.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">8) Dark Thaumaturgy practiced by Baali, Angellis Ater, and practically every infernalist.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">9) Wanga practiced by a couple Samedi vampires, but used to a greater degree by the Serpents of Light.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">10) Anarch Sorcery that includes 4 different &quot;Waves&quot; (Think of them as different schools) practiced by the Anarchs.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">11) Sihr practiced by Islamic kindred.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I see no issue with this, sure this kind of downplays the clans who have Blood Magic as a big part of their backstory, such as the Tremere, but I feel like this gives you a lot of options to create a story that is more heavily focused on the Supernatural side of VTM. I always felt the conflict between different blood magic clans and bloodlines was underdeveloped. It would have loved to see two different blood magicians battle over the ownership of a certain spirit, or something similar to that. It doesn't have to be a violent conflict either. They could just make a deal for shared ownership of it.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It would also have been pretty interesting if we could have seen how the different Blood Magic Traditions view each other. Do the Assamite Sorcery suspect Kolduns of practicing infernalism? Do Kolduns think that Assamite Sorcery is outdated, and that Koldunic Sorcery is a newer, better version of Dur-An-Ki? How do different Clans and Bloodlines that are known for practicing Necromancy feel about Sadhana? How do the practitioners of Sadhana feel about Necromancy? I just find stuff like this really interesting and I feel it would really add more depth to the many Factions who are known for practicing Blood Magic.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">But maybe I'm wrong, maybe having so many Blood Magic Traditions harms the game as a whole.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u200bWhat do you think?</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":27313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","user":"Hello","date":". 07-19-2022, 02:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T16:38:57-07:00","id":1486809,"title":"","content":"I think it's worth looking at the difference between who has <b>access</b> to Blood Magic, and who has <b>In-Clan</b> Blood Magic. There are very few Disciplines that are hard to access (and most of those are because they're attached to a rare Bloodline). Even Discipline very associated with certain Clans (Protean, Obtenebration, Vicissitude, etc) can end up in other Clan hand even if not wildly taught. Toreador that want to learn the early levels of Vicissitude to do various kinds of &quot;living&quot; art on undead flesh can do that if they know the right Toreador rather than asking a Tzimisce for it.<br /> <br /> When a Clan or Bloodline has Blood Magic as In-Clan it not only impacts the XP value, but also the ease of learning as you don't to blood bond yourself to a tutor. The vast majority of Setites have access to Blood Magic, but would still have to learn it like any other Out of Clan Discipline even if they can negotiate to learn from another Setite.<br /> <br /> Access to Blood Magic grew a lot over the course of the original VtM run for sure, but also far more than In-Clan groups of Blood Sorcerers, which gives groups like the Tremere an edge.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T16:54:29-07:00","id":1486811,"title":"","content":"As a rule of thumb I think the in-lore growth of Blood Magic is a good thing. It makes sense and it is an easy way to expand both powers and culture of a clan without breaking usual Discipline &quot;economy&quot;, so to speak (more than it was already broken).<br /> <br /> I also don't think it downplays anyone because Magic Traditions have the accompanying point of exploring styles, outlooks and theories behind the power as a means to explore the differences between groups. They don't play the same, don't have similar roles in the game and do not feel redundant even if they're all Magicians. Quite the opposite, Blood Magic arguably did a better job at making them shine as distinct clans than their own signature Disciplines for the Banu Haqim, Setites and maybe even Tzimisce (depending on who you ask this). I see no one claiming that Dur-An-Ki, Akhu and Koldunic Sorcery just made them seem too much like Tremere.<br /> <br /> There is a caveat, but it is not the concept of Blood Magic and, instead, its rules. While perception on this problem varies, there are many concerns with it for balance and the feel of the mechanics. But such is the problem that it remains in place even if you only have the Tremere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T17:04:31-07:00","id":1486813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486804-blood-magic-at-this-point-is-extremely-common?p=1486809#post1486809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When a Clan or Bloodline has Blood Magic as In-Clan it not only impacts the XP value, but also the ease of learning as you don't to blood bond yourself to a tutor. The vast majority of Setites have access to Blood Magic, but would still have to learn it like any other Out of Clan Discipline even if they can negotiate to learn from another Setite.<br /> <br /> Access to Blood Magic grew a lot over the course of the original VtM run for sure, but also far more than In-Clan groups of Blood Sorcerers, which gives groups like the Tremere an edge.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I was under the impression that Blood Magic was learned more through active study instead of through blood bond.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T17:58:10-07:00","id":1486815,"title":"","content":"I actually dealt with this in my games by personalization.<br /> <br /> This is basically an in-universe conversation I had with the PCs that is recreated here and does a better job than an OOC explanation:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;The thing you've got to understand is that vampire numbers are pretty damn small so when people use generalities, they miss the subtleties of what is exactly being said. What do I mean, exactly, what I mean is that the Tremere have Blood Magic. It is a part of them and if every Tremere in the world but ten died, they'd be able to restart because it comes naturally to them.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Other clans have Blood Magic but that's misleading. What they have are members who<u> have </u>Blood Magic.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;There's exceptions to this like the Assamite Sorcerer Bloodline but that's like three hundred guys. A good chunk of the Clan but when we talk about things like Setite Sorcery or Tzimisce Kolduns, we're talking about maybe thirty guys each and that's being incredibly generous. These people have their own ancient forms of magic cultivated over centuries but every single one of them probably knows one another. You want to know Koldun magic, you go to a guy who studied under a guy who learned it from Yorak who made it over three thousand years. Everyone else? Five or six guys and sometimes these mage groups get wiped out once their leader goes.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Every Clan has a sorcerer or two among them, despite the Tremere's efforts. The Nosferatu had the Baba Yagas who all learned from one of her descendants and are the inspiration for every Wicked Witch of the East, West, North, and South. Be glad the Inquisition and werewolves got most of them in the Dark Ages. Now? You can't find any of that once-large cult. They died with the Hag. You want to learn Lasombra magic, go talk to Lucien Sejanus if you can find him or his daughters. Ventrue magic? Find one of Mithras' cult. Why? Because every Ventrue who knows blood magic learned it from Mithras or one of his students.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;There are best not thought of Clan magics but individual vampires who have old as shit names. And no, Necromancy isn't blood magic. It's Necromancy.&quot;</i></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 07-17-2022, 09:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T18:30:52-07:00","id":1486817,"title":"","content":"Every WoD splat seems to have one area where the devs shoe horn all the extra ideas they have. In Exalted 2nd it was Martial Arts styles, in Werewolf it was endless charm lists, in Vampire it was the paths of magic/necromancy.<br /> <br /> From a design standpoint, this is atrocious. It displays a lack of preplanning and too many cooks in the kitchen kind of scenario.<br /> <br /> As for magic paths in Vampire, with each new clan/bloodline reveal, the history was retconned, which meant things made progressively less and less sense. Between the Tzimisce, the Setites, the Assamites, and the Cappadocians, is there any real reason for the Tremere to be considered special for their magic? Perhaps I am a bit jaded because when I started playing, none of the clans/bloodlines outside of the core 7 were named, let alone given backstories or disciplines.<br /> <br /> All in all the situation reeks of every new thing contain the cool parts of previous things. While some may look at that and exclaim &quot;build variety&quot; I look at it and say that all that was achieved was making everything the same. Any clan can be anything, which results in a lack of clan and bloodline identity if the writers are not careful.<br /> <br /> Think of it like playing an FPS, both sides have the same weapons, the same movement abilities, the same mechanics, and the same map goals. The only difference is a character skin or Team Color designation. Very much Red vs. Blue rather than anything deeper in game play or design. On the other hand, if you take something like AvP, which is an asymmetrical FPS game, each faction has different play styles, different gear, different goals.<br /> <br /> So yeah, excessive magic bloat means the &quot;blandification&quot; of vampire in general and one hell of an XP sink for anyone who wants to &quot;master magic&quot; as a build.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T18:39:19-07:00","id":1486819,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that seems about right to me Phipps. There's a couple of groups who have Blood Magic as an in-clan Discipline, but they're very small (Assamite Sorcerer Caste) or they're extinct (Witches of Echidna). In every case, while there are blood sorcerers who don't have blood magic as an in-clan Discipline among every clan, those blood sorcerers make up a distinct minority of the clan. Only among the Assamites and the Tzimisci are blood mages common enough to have their own distinct customs within the greater clan. Even the within the Lasombra, the Abyss Mystics don't really have a distinct clan culture apart from the rest and the same is true of Setite Sorcerers. They're just Lasombra or Setites who practice magic, and there's not enough of them to have a major impact within the greater clan.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile with the Tremere, blood sorcerers are in the distinct majority. In fact, any Tremere who doesn't practice blood sorcery is likely to himself unable to rise up the ranks or earn the respect of his peers. They are, by far and away, the most powerful blood sorcerers among the kindred. And like you said, since blood sorcery is an in-clan Discipline for them, any Tremere could recreate or create a blood magic path far easier than someone who doesn't have blood sorcery as a clan Discipline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T18:52:22-07:00","id":1486822,"title":"","content":"<b>CT Phipps Blood Sorcery House Rules</b><br /> <br /> I also added these rules to spruce up the lore of Blood Sorcery in my games.<br /> <br /> * No vampire can learn Blood Sorcery unless he had magical potential while alive, diablerizes a vampire with Blood Sorcery, or is one of the Tremere or Assamite Sorcerer Bloodlines.<br /> <br /> * Necromancy and Blood Sorcery are fundamentally different disciplines. Learning one gives no advantage to learning the other.<br /> <br /> * The exception to learning Blood Sorcery is if you make a demonic pact. Dark Thaumaturgy and Koldunism are really two sides of the same coin here as the latter requires a pact with Kupala or one of their minions. Setites also learn their magic by making pacts with Apophis, which Silent Striders claim is just straight up Wyrm magic.<br /> <br /> * Infernalism is pretty damn rare but it is the easiest, quickest, and actually most common way for a &quot;normal&quot; vampire to learn magic. No natural spirit, angel, or Aeon will deal with vampires.<br /> <br /> * Vampires cannot learn Hedge Magic from mortals. Any vampire who is Embraced loses both true and hedge magic but not psychic Numina. They may have a much easier time learning basic disciplines.<br /> <br /> * A Embraced Awakened mage does have the potential to learn Blood Sorcery, small consolation as that may be. They also &quot;attract&quot; demons like a fly zapper and are a major source of Infernalists.<br /> <br /> * Demons can visit vampires with magical potential in their dreams (which most vampires don't have). The Tremere generally tell you to ignore them.<br /> <br /> * Aside from PCs breaking the rules for storytelling purposes, it requires a minimum of ten years of study to learn Blood Sorcery 1. Most Tremere Neonates have been studying thirty years and are fairly &quot;old&quot; Neonates by the time they're released.<br /> <br /> * A Blood Sorcery 3 level is usually at least 50 years of study. Another reason the Tremere spend all of their time reading in their chantries. 5 is something that often takes a full century to reach and is a sign you are an Elder of the Clan.<br /> <br /> * Even if a vampire were to acquire Tremere books of magic, they'd be useless due to the requirements above. It requires a massive grounding in philosophy, mindset, meditation, practice, and equipment to use magic.<br /> <br /> * Despite how awesome Blood Sorcery is and can be, it is really a lifetime vocation and vampires aren't as impressed with it generally as the Tremere's players/Tremere themselves are. Few undead are able to make the commitment even if somehow offered.<br /> <br /> * Lots of vampires have mysticism about their Disciplines so there's a mystical flare to studying everything from Dementation/Dominate to Oblivion to Vicissitude.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 07-17-2022, 09:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T19:02:58-07:00","id":1486826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486804-blood-magic-at-this-point-is-extremely-common?p=1486819#post1486819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, that seems about right to me Phipps. There's a couple of groups who have Blood Magic as an in-clan Discipline, but they're very small (Assamite Sorcerer Caste) or they're extinct (Witches of Echidna). In every case, while there are blood sorcerers who don't have blood magic as an in-clan Discipline among every clan, those blood sorcerers make up a distinct minority of the clan. Only among the Assamites and the Tzimisci are blood mages common enough to have their own distinct customs within the greater clan. Even the within the Lasombra, the Abyss Mystics don't really have a distinct clan culture apart from the rest and the same is true of Setite Sorcerers. They're just Lasombra or Setites who practice magic, and there's not enough of them to have a major impact within the greater clan.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile with the Tremere, blood sorcerers are in the distinct majority. In fact, any Tremere who doesn't practice blood sorcery is likely to himself unable to rise up the ranks or earn the respect of his peers. They are, by far and away, the most powerful blood sorcerers among the kindred. And like you said, since blood sorcery is an in-clan Discipline for them, any Tremere could recreate or create a blood magic path far easier than someone who doesn't have blood sorcery as a clan Discipline.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, definitely what I was going for.<br /> <br /> Funny fact, I actually have a name for the non-Thaumaturgy-using Tremere in my games. They're called the Brights.<br /> <br /> <b>&quot;Brights&quot;</b><br /> <br /> The idea that sometimes the Tremere make a &quot;mistake&quot; in Embracing into their Clan with a charlatan, poor choice, or (worse) romantic attachment. Brights are someone the Clan used to execute outright but have since found a place for at the bottom of the Pyramid. These Tremere usually aren't STUPID by any stretch of the imagination and have other qualities than magical potential. So, they are used by the Tremere to gather power the more traditional way with their Auspex and Dominate abilities. They're often heavily involved in court politics and Kindred affairs, many times getting large amounts of status and playing political games. Sometimes, they're even made the Princes of cities.<br /> <br /> All the while, other Camarilla members never suspect how much disdain they're held by the rest of the Clan.<br /> <br /> In V5, I stated the Brights are now actually a power block because none of them died in the Vienna strike. Unfortunately, their whining does very little as long as Schrekt is the head of House Tremere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T19:35:42-07:00","id":1486829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486804-blood-magic-at-this-point-is-extremely-common?p=1486813#post1486813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I was under the impression that Blood Magic was learned more through active study instead of through blood bond.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the most common examples are Tremere Banu Hakim sorcerers, or Giovanni/Cappadocians/Hecata necromancers: they're learning their In-Clan Discipline and thus don't have the blood drinking requirement.<br /> <br /> There's nothing in the rules about learning Disciplines that exempts Blood Magic. If a Brujah wants to learn Thaumaturgy, they have to drink from their tutor on top of instruction. If a Tremere wants to learn Necromancy/Oblivion... same thing.<br /> <br /> Which is actually a fairly meaningful difference despite being a small one.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T21:10:40-07:00","id":1486837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486804-blood-magic-at-this-point-is-extremely-common?p=1486822#post1486822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>CT Phipps Blood Sorcery House Rules</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I find it interesting to have this general kind of house-rules that help define what Magic is in yout game, but I disagree with almost every one of your options. Which isn't a problem, it just highlights that Magic can be different things for different games.<br /> <br /> My own default (I'm never against changing my setting for a new chronicle) would be somewhat different:<ul><li>Blood Magic is a property of Vitae, but need knowledge and effort to distill. No vampire has it as In-Clan (having only two In-Clans is the Tremere Weakness in my games currently);</li> <li>Necromancy is special because affects things too close to the vampire's nature. It is still Blood Magic, but has distinct personal consequences;</li> <li>Deriving Magic from the outside, like spiritual pacts, brings a host of its own consequences, but a wise Magician will take time to study and make benign pacts which the end result being effectively indistinguishable from regular Blood Magic or even be healthier, so to speak. Only a fool or someone who purposefully walks such a path will reek of the Wyrm;</li> <li>Vampires can deal with all sorts of spirits if they know how to do so, which is tricky but doable. Those who chose the easier pacts, though, end up either as infernalists or under the power of entities that do not have their well-being in mind, from dangerous demons to spirits that demand constant and exacting service;</li> <li>Hedge Magic is the basis for Blood Magic. While it doesn't work straight up for vampires, it is easy to convert into a new Blood Magic Path, as many magicians proved throughout time;</li> <li>An Embraced Awakened has an Entrapped Avatar, unable to grant True Magic, but also to reincarnate. Yet this being still exists and can be contacted for knowledge and pacts with the right magic;</li> <li>Contacting demons is rare, infernalism is a knowledge hunted and buried beneath ignorance, persecution and lies. But it is stupidly easy to actually perform and requires almost no deeper knowledge, even if the thing summoned praises you for your skill at research and ritual preparation. This is just hollow praise, it is almost impossible to truly botch the summoning. It isn't so hard to botch doing it safely, though;</li> <li>Time of study depends on several factors, including magical style. Tremere Hermeticism is the most demanding style to master any level, serving as the upper bar. Under typical circumstances, which means about 2 or 3 hours/night dedicated to study and no greater talent than the interest in the topic, it takes Level\u00b2 in <u>decades</u> to master any given level from 0. While there's no bottom line for learning times, it would take a true genius with everything stacked at their favor and almost total dedication to study to cut this time to a tenth without relying on any weird factor, but is possible;</li> <li>With this in mind you can expect any active Tremere with more than 3 dots to be an Elder. Many active Neonates actually do not have even their first dot yet, and the clan has both active members that do not spend too much time studying (they still study magic a lot, to be honest, as they study 2 or 3 hours <i>every single night</i>), and shut-ins completely dedicated to master magic in a sensible time scale;</li> <li>Studying Magic from zero from books is possible, but time-consuming and fraught with dangers. Yet the best source to do so would be a Tremere library if it is complete enough, as those are meant to have everything you need. Were the Tremere wiped-out at once, their whole brand of Magic would still be possible for any inheritor of their libraries to reconstruct;</li> <li>It takes time, effort and/or risk to learn Magic, you can't have it without paying the toll in some way. It is also worth noting that this isn't really a path to greater understanding of the mysteries of the Blood or its supernatural powers, just a means to extract its innate magic and apply somewhere else;</li> <li>You can derive a particular brand of magic from any Discipline in the same way the Lasombra did with <b>Obtenebration</b>.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486804-blood-magic-at-this-point-is-extremely-common?p=1486826#post1486826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're called the Brights.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't run it like this, I think even in the beginning the Tremere would find it a waste to just destroy or shove to the side those who aren't very good at Magic.<br /> <br /> Even at their time at the Order of Hermes, people who just believed in their system and helped the House were an important part of it, as it is in every Mage Tradition. This wouldn't change into unlife, as long as the &quot;lost cause&quot; student gives to the clan and do their best for their Magocracy, they're a perfectly good pair of hands and speaking mouth to do something for the clan. Specially in their times as a minor bloodline with too many enemies they would need those people.<br /> <br /> Completely shutting them from any raise in power would also be a long term problem as it just creates resentment in people that may be better at it in the future. Again, they're from a background where people could Awaken at any point in time, so even your worse students could at some point become bright stars if they're just incompetent at magic instead of actual liabilities. You also needs the underlings for all your good students to lord over.<br /> <br /> My take is that non-Thaumaturges among the Tremere have their own hierarchy depending on their role and feats. This will never put them in a high station by itself, but they can measure against themselves and against at least Fledglings and Neonates. But as time goes on, if they don't learn Magic then they'll be able to surpass only those magicians who stagnate early (which is a thing), and even then only if they keep up their work. It is increasingly rare to see such cases, though, only if they have insurmountable problems with magical learning or are fine with a minor, unremarkable position within the clan, because otherwise it's only a matter of time and <i>some</i> study for even them to learn Blood Magic.<br /> <br /> An important caveat: any such Tremere who achieves power and success outside the clan isn't just derided anymore. While they may still have a low rank within due to lack of Magic, their resources are still too useful for the clan and too dangerous against it to be ignored. They don't need rank necessarily to use their power to obtain favors, have magicians trying to ingratiate themselves to them or even have some really prestigious teachers offering to help with their occult training. It isn't the same thing as the prestige of actually being good at Magic, but depending on circumstances and the person is good enough a substitute.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T02:32:18-07:00","id":1486858,"title":"","content":"I see no issue with this, sure this kind of downplays the clans who have Blood Magic as a big part of their backstory, such as the Tremere, [/quote]<br /> I don't think it does. The Tremere became dominant, and will remain dominant, because their method and organization has very signficant advantages over others.<br /> <br /> 1: Other Thaumarturges need to look over their shoulders to keep their precious secrets all the time, with limited resources. Maybe someone will blood bond into a pocket magician. The Tremere can practice easily in well stocked and well fortified chantries and have the backing of the Tremere.<br /> 2: Tremere organization allows them to be interdependent and specialize in specific fields, greatly increasing the diversity and amount of favours the chantry can wrack in as a group. Without such unity Non-Tremere can't specialize this way and retread a lot of the same ground their competitors do.<br /> 3: The Tremere share an excellent library and a practice that is easy to teach. Your average anarch thaumaturge will be lucky to have enough writings to learn three different paths, mostly having to go through the excrutiating process of reinventing each path or ritual. Despite being far more ancient, Assamites have a library half as good; their idiosyncratic style makes sharing knowledge and finding a good teacher hard.<br /> 4: Tremere have an in clan discount for thaumaturgy and have a reasonable chance to reach the 5th level before 100 years. Learning 2-3 levels of an out-of-clan discipline is taxing, getting to 4+ exorbitant for young vampires<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> but I feel like this gives you a lot of options to create a story that is more heavily focused on the Supernatural side of VTM. I always felt the conflict between different blood magic clans and bloodlines was underdeveloped. It would have loved to see two different blood magicians battle over the ownership of a certain spirit, or something similar to that. It doesn't have to be a violent conflict either. They could just make a deal for shared ownership of it. </div> </div> </div>The problem here iss Tremere dominance, but in other cases i agree.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It would also have been pretty interesting if we could have seen how the different Blood Magic Traditions view each other. Do the Assamite Sorcery suspect Kolduns of practicing infernalism? </div> </div> </div>Every Thaumaturge convinces themselves that their tradition is best.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486804-blood-magic-at-this-point-is-extremely-common?p=1486822#post1486822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>CT Phipps Blood Sorcery House Rules</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Hard NO to a lot of things here<br /> <br /> My own rules: <br /> -Thaumaturgy is a discipline of the soul, the blood is just a convenient power source: everyone can do it, unless there's something deeply wrong with you. Vampires can do it, mortals can do it, Thinbloods can do it, Werewolves can do it* (I'm on the fence when it comes to Mages) Mortals would need to sacrifice something to pull it off or find a roundabout method to power such magic.<br /> <i>*Werewolves are very unlikely to learn it given the cost-effective convenience of gifts and cultural values. Ronin would likely be the only users. </i><br /> <br /> -<b>Paradigm</b> matters. A practitioner without a magical bloodline needs a minimum of 3 dots of occult or equivalent to properly internalize the belief system needed to use Thaumaturgy. (I would encourage it for those with a magical bloodline) <br /> <br /> Dark Thaumaturgy adds onto Thaumaturgy/ Equivalents up to your generational maximum+1 (Necromancy/Koldunic sorcery/Abyss mysticism aren't thaumaturgy, everything else is) If you have 3 thaumaturgy, rather than buying dots 4 and 5, buying Dark thaumaturgy 1/2 would be a cheaper way to get to 4th and 5th level magic. Also, DT is always at in-clan costs (x5 for Caitiff too). <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 07-18-2022, 07:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T02:51:39-07:00","id":1486859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486804-blood-magic-at-this-point-is-extremely-common?p=1486858#post1486858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Thaumaturgy is a discipline of the soul, the blood is just a convenient power source: everyone can do it, unless there's something deeply wrong with you. Vampires can do it, mortals can do it, Thinbloods can do it, Werewolves can do it* (I'm on the fence when it comes to Mages) Mortals would need to sacrifice something to pull it off or find a roundabout method to power such magic.<br /> <i>*Werewolves are very unlikely to learn it given the cost-effective convenience of gifts and cultural values. Ronin would likely be the only users. </i><br /> <br /> -<b>Paradigm</b> matters. A practitioner without a magical bloodline needs a minimum of 3 dots of occult or equivalent to properly internalize the belief system needed to use Thaumaturgy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and vampires by having their avatars shattered do not have the benefit that humans do of having Thaumaturgy being something they can easily learn.<br /> <br /> Hence why vampirism is a curse among other things.<br /> <br /> The ease for which it flows for the Tremere is something truly special and unprecedented.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T04:57:53-07:00","id":1486865,"title":"","content":"Ehhh, for me, blood magic is <i>blood</i> magic. It's powered by a vampire's blood. Whether the vampire used to have an Avatar or whatever is irrelevant. Now they have vampire blood and they use that to power their magic. As such, any vampire could learn blood magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T06:23:24-07:00","id":1486872,"title":"","content":"&quot;Blood Magic&quot; is a misnomer that leads people into doing... what was done in V5. blood themed bloody blood magic. W5 will have us use wolfy wolf-moon magic, yeah?<br /> <br /> Thaumaturgy, the creation of miracles, better describes the various styles of Magic Discipline: control plants, create fires, conjure objects, deliver curses, change the weather, merge with machines.. these are miracles. We can contrast it with Protean: If Protean is a power that draws from the Beast to become a beast, Thaumaturgy is a power of enlightenment that elevates man above beast; Indeed, it's not actually usable when in frenzy, because it's not a power that really belongs to the state of being a Vampire. Above all It's a power that requires Will and Knowledge, something the Beast utterly lacks. Metaphysically, the acquisition of such higher power is a search for becoming one with a God or the Universe, to be more than just a man or a vampire. To take all this down and fucking limit it to &quot;Blood magic&quot; is a gross injustice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T10:40:54-07:00","id":1486888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486804-blood-magic-at-this-point-is-extremely-common?p=1486817#post1486817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every WoD splat seems to have one area where the devs shoe horn all the extra ideas they have. In Exalted 2nd it was Martial Arts styles, in Werewolf it was endless charm lists, in Vampire it was the paths of magic/necromancy.<br /> <br /> From a design standpoint, this is atrocious. It displays a lack of preplanning and too many cooks in the kitchen kind of scenario.<br /> <br /> As for magic paths in Vampire, with each new clan/bloodline reveal, the history was retconned, which meant things made progressively less and less sense. Between the Tzimisce, the Setites, the Assamites, and the Cappadocians, is there any real reason for the Tremere to be considered special for their magic? Perhaps I am a bit jaded because when I started playing, none of the clans/bloodlines outside of the core 7 were named, let alone given backstories or disciplines.<br /> <br /> All in all the situation reeks of every new thing contain the cool parts of previous things. While some may look at that and exclaim &amp;quot;build variety&amp;quot; I look at it and say that all that was achieved was making everything the same. Any clan can be anything, which results in a lack of clan and bloodline identity if the writers are not careful.<br /> <br /> Think of it like playing an FPS, both sides have the same weapons, the same movement abilities, the same mechanics, and the same map goals. The only difference is a character skin or Team Color designation. Very much Red vs. Blue rather than anything deeper in game play or design. On the other hand, if you take something like AvP, which is an asymmetrical FPS game, each faction has different play styles, different gear, different goals.<br /> <br /> So yeah, excessive magic bloat means the &amp;quot;blandification&amp;quot; of vampire in general and one hell of an XP sink for anyone who wants to &amp;quot;master magic&amp;quot; as a build.</div> </div> </div> </div>I absolutely HATE and utterly DESPISE Blood Magic in all forms, and more and more of it with each new supplement of &quot;new bag of cool tricks&quot; that is published. Just as much as I absolutely hate and despise all the bloodlines bag of endless weird. Oh, and the tons of nonsensical exclusive disciplines with powers that are each time more and more taken completely out of the ass. VtM just turned into a cartoonish carnival of nonsense because of those.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T12:22:06-07:00","id":1486893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486804-blood-magic-at-this-point-is-extremely-common?p=1486865#post1486865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ehhh, for me, blood magic is <i>blood</i> magic. It's powered by a vampire's blood. Whether the vampire used to have an Avatar or whatever is irrelevant. Now they have vampire blood and they use that to power their magic. As such, any vampire could learn blood magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, that just makes it way too common in my opinion.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T12:48:40-07:00","id":1486899,"title":"","content":"Part of the issue can be traced back to the original Thaumaturgy paths in first edition. Basically, they were treated as an expansion of powers that could be added because no individual clan discipline set could cover all vampire powers in media at the time.<br /> <br /> Dracula may have originally been officially statted out as a Tzimisce, but you need Lure of Flames, Weather Control, and Movement of the Mind to complete the power set. But even if you convert those Paths to straight up disciplines, that would mean either giving every clan 6 disciplines or creating a system where there were always generic disciplines that were not associated by clans that could be picked up on the cheap.<br /> <br /> It might have worked better if WW kept Thaumturgy as a singular path with a ton of rituals, rather than adding on tons of paths. But I doubt that would have been any better than a stop gap measure of design.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T12:51:58-07:00","id":1486900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486804-blood-magic-at-this-point-is-extremely-common?p=1486888#post1486888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I absolutely HATE and utterly DESPISE Blood Magic in all forms, and more and more of it with each new supplement of &quot;new bag of cool tricks&quot; that is published. Just as much as I absolutely hate and despise all the bloodlines bag of endless weird. Oh, and the tons of nonsensical exclusive disciplines with powers that are each time more and more taken completely out of the ass. VtM just turned into a cartoonish carnival of nonsense because of those.</div> </div> </div> </div>By chance have you looked into Kindred of the East? That design of things might be more to your liking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T12:56:02-07:00","id":1486902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486804-blood-magic-at-this-point-is-extremely-common?p=1486899#post1486899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It might have worked better if WW kept Thaumturgy as a singular path with a ton of rituals, rather than adding on tons of paths. But I doubt that would have been any better than a stop gap measure of design.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's just what V5 Blood Sorcery is, no? Path of Blood + Quietus as the main &quot;Path&quot; and an assortment of rituals covering anything else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T13:40:43-07:00","id":1486907,"title":"","content":"In my opinion, vampires should have SOMETHING that allows them to duplicate classic Dracula powers like weather-control, making doors open and close, and making all the candles in a room light or snuff. However, I really don't care how that is achieved. If you want to get rid of Thaumaturgy all together, and make those powers a choice from the other disciplines, I'm fine with that.<br /> <br /> Maybe weather-control could be a Dominate power where you master it to such a degree that you can control the weather. Or an Oblivion power where you pull the chaos of the underworld's maelstrom into the physical realm causing a thunderstorm. Or an Animalism power where you send the rage of your beast into the atmosphere causing a raging thunderstorm.<br /> <br /> I really give zero F's how you get there, I just want to control the effing weather like Dracula. I want to shout &quot;vinds! VIIINDS!! VIIIIIIIINDS!!!&quot; and have the winds obey me. Could not care less about the mechanical details that get me this classic ability. Just get it done in some form.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T14:54:27-07:00","id":1486913,"title":"","content":"I think doing it as a ritual is the best option, or at least the least silly one from the ones you listed. (Doing it with oblivion sounds obscenely destructive though, through all the spectres and what not)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T15:02:55-07:00","id":1486914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486804-blood-magic-at-this-point-is-extremely-common?p=1486907#post1486907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my opinion, vampires should have SOMETHING that allows them to duplicate classic Dracula powers like weather-control, making doors open and close, and making all the candles in a room light or snuff. However, I really don't care how that is achieved. If you want to get rid of Thaumaturgy all together, and make those powers a choice from the other disciplines, I'm fine with that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Odd fact: All of these are not Dracula's vampire powers.<br /> <br /> They are, in fact, his MAGIC powers.<br /> <br /> Dracula's abilities in the book include some from being a Nosferatu but the majority is him doing sorcery that he learned at the Scholomance from the Devil.<br /> <br /> Dracula being a Tremere is thus entirely justifiable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T15:07:57-07:00","id":1486915,"title":"","content":"Is that specified? I recall it being said that he learned from Scholomance, but it was left utterly vague which powers were innate to being a vampire and which were learned. But then it's been a long time since I read Dracula. Can you quote the part that specifies this so precisely?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T15:20:45-07:00","id":1486918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486804-blood-magic-at-this-point-is-extremely-common?p=1486915#post1486915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is that specified? I recall it being said that he learned from Scholomance, but it was left utterly vague which powers were innate to being a vampire and which were learned. But then it's been a long time since I read Dracula. Can you quote the part that specifies this so precisely?</div> </div> </div> </div>I appear to have been wrong as it doesn't say what is from sorcery and what is from being a vampire. I actually think the text is implying Dracula is a vampire because of his sorcery, though, rather than a condition he inherited, though. So it may be a distinction without a difference within Dracula.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;The vampire live on, and cannot die by mere passing of the time; he can flourish when that he can fatten on the blood of the living. Even more, we have seen amongst us that he can even grow younger; that his vital faculties grow strenuous, and seem as though they refresh themselves when his special pabulum is plenty. But he cannot flourish without this diet; he eat not as others. Even friend Jonathan, who lived with him for weeks, did never see him to eat, never! He throws no shadow; he make in the mirror no reflect, as again Jonathan observe. He has the strength of many of his hand\u2014witness again Jonathan when he shut the door against the wolfs, and when he help him from the diligence too. He can transform himself to wolf, as we gather from the ship arrival in Whitby, when he tear open the dog; he can be as bat, as Madam Mina saw him on the window at Whitby, and as friend John saw him fly from this so near house, and as my friend Quincey saw him at the window of Miss Lucy. He can come in mist which he create\u2014that noble ship\u2019s captain proved him of this; but, from what we know, the distance he can make this mist is limited, and it can only be round himself. He come on moonlight rays as elemental dust\u2014as again Jonathan saw those sisters in the castle of Dracula. He become so small\u2014we ourselves saw Miss Lucy, ere she was at peace, slip through a hairbreadth space at the tomb door. He can, when once he find his way, come out from anything or into anything, no matter how close it be bound or even fused up with fire\u2014solder you call it. He can see in the dark\u2014no small power this, in a world which is one half shut from the light. Ah, but hear me through. He can do all these things, yet he is not free. Nay; he is even more prisoner than the slave of the galley, than the madman in his cell. He cannot go where he lists; he who is not of nature has yet to obey some of nature\u2019s laws\u2014why we know not. He may not enter anywhere at the first, unless there be some one of the household who bid him to come; though afterwards he can come as he please. His power ceases, as does that of all evil things, at the coming of the day. Only at certain times can he have limited freedom. If he be not at the place whither he is bound, he can only change himself at noon or at exact sunrise or sunset. These things are we told, and in this record of ours we have proof by inference. Thus, whereas he can do as he will within his limit, when he have his earth-home, his coffin-home, his hell-home, the place unhallowed, as we saw when he went to the grave of the suicide at Whitby; still at other time he can only change when the time come. It is said, too, that he can only pass running water at the slack or the flood of the tide. Then there are things which so afflict him that he has no power, as the garlic that we know of; and as for things sacred, as this symbol, my crucifix, that was amongst us even now when we resolve, to them he is nothing, but in their presence he take his place far off and silent with respect. There are others, too, which I shall tell you of, lest in our seeking we may need them. The branch of wild rose on his coffin keep him that he move not from it; a sacred bullet fired into the coffin kill him so that he be true dead; and as for the stake through him, we know already of its peace; or the cut-off head that giveth rest. We have seen it with our eyes&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cThus when we find the habitation of this man-that-was, we can confine him to his coffin and destroy him, if we obey what we know. But he is clever. I have asked my friend Arminius, of Buda-Pesth University, to make his record; and, from all the means that are, he tell me of what he has been. He must, indeed, have been that Voivode Dracula who won his name against the Turk, over the great river on the very frontier of Turkey-land. If it be so, then was he no common man; for in that time, and for centuries after, he was spoken of as the cleverest and the most cunning, as well as the bravest of the sons of the \u2018land beyond the forest.\u2019 That mighty brain and that iron resolution went with him to his grave, and are even now arrayed against us. <b>The Draculas were, says Arminius, a great and noble race, though now and again were scions who were held by their coevals to have had dealings with the Evil One. They learned his secrets in the Scholomance, amongst the mountains over Lake Hermanstadt, where the devil claims the tenth scholar as his due. In the records are such words as \u2018stregoica\u2019\u2014witch, \u2018ordog,\u2019 and \u2018pokol\u2019\u2014Satan and hell; and in one manuscript this very Dracula is spoken of as \u2018wampyr,</b>\u2019 which we all understand too well. There have been from the loins of this very one great men and good women, and their graves make sacred the earth where alone this foulness can dwell. For it is not the least of its terrors that this evil thing is rooted deep in all good; in soil barren of holy memories it cannot rest.\u201d</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T20:11:39-07:00","id":1486939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486804-blood-magic-at-this-point-is-extremely-common?p=1486859#post1486859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The ease for which it flows for the Tremere is something truly special and unprecedented.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not unprecedented if the Banu Haqim Sorcerers do it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486804-blood-magic-at-this-point-is-extremely-common?p=1486872#post1486872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Blood Magic&quot; is a misnomer that leads people into doing... what was done in V5. blood themed bloody blood magic. W5 will have us use wolfy wolf-moon magic, yeah?</div> </div> </div> </div>I only partially disagree. The part about vampire magic being solely blood-themed is quite stupid.<br /> <br /> But to borrow now directly from Mage and shorten the explanation, my take is that Vitae is too powerful as a source of Quintessence, and that's what makes magic distinct for vampires, considering that the lore overtly states that magic <b>is</b> distinct for vampires, because while mortal magicians have a clear head start to practice they always had to adapt.<br /> <br /> Simply put, the presence of Vitae both somewhats hinder vampires from working magic as usual (possibly because their own Curse and Blood creates some kind of magical interference), but also offers them a readily available source of Tass. Whatever Paradigm they use, they have to adapt to this very specific Tass, hence they all have a cost in Blood. But you're not bloodily bloodying every bloody thing you put your bloodied hands on to perform magic, while you're constrained to always using this Tass, you have the advantage of this thing being a part of you and under your significant control, so this cost may very well be you meditating or whatever to distill the actual Quintessence you'll use out of the Blood to turn it into a form you can actually work with.<br /> <br /> Vampires are quite simply and directly the most effective Quintessence-producing Alchemical furnace in the setting, turning common blood into pure magic and then burning it at will for various tasks. That's why their magic come from their blood even when it is not blood-themed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486804-blood-magic-at-this-point-is-extremely-common?p=1486899#post1486899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Part of the issue can be traced back to the original Thaumaturgy paths in first edition. Basically, they were treated as an expansion of powers that could be added because no individual clan discipline set could cover all vampire powers in media at the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it's not that. Or at least, not just that.<br /> <br /> Vampire-wizards is almost as old a trope as vampires themselves, and that includes Dracula. Since the original novel and in many of his movie adaptations some of his powers are sorcery, not innate extensions of his condition as an undead. Actually it is possible that most are spells as far as the original novel goes. It has also Evil-Hogwarts and other witchcraft-related whatnot.<br /> <br /> The Tremere are as much a core vampire archetype as the other Seven Clans, and Thaumaturgy just as much a trope-power for vampires to wield, and that's actually one of my reasons to let any vampire learn it if they put the effort and pay the price.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":5826,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","user":"monteparnas","date":". 07-18-2022, 11:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T23:23:34-07:00","id":1486967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486804-blood-magic-at-this-point-is-extremely-common?p=1486939#post1486939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Simply put, the presence of Vitae both somewhats hinder vampires from working magic as usual (possibly because their own Curse and Blood creates some kind of magical interference), but also offers them a readily available source of Tass. Whatever Paradigm they use, they have to adapt to this very specific Tass, hence they all have a cost in Blood. .</div> </div> </div> </div>Rituals rarely require blood. There are also one or two powers that let you get around using your blood pool, though I can't remember where they are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-19T00:16:46-07:00","id":1486970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486804-blood-magic-at-this-point-is-extremely-common?p=1486967#post1486967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rituals rarely require blood. There are also one or two powers that let you get around using your blood pool, though I can't remember where they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know Akhu allows Followers of Set to craft an altar that lets them cast Sorcery without needing to expend vitae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-19T06:59:28-07:00","id":1487001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486804-blood-magic-at-this-point-is-extremely-common?p=1486967#post1486967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rituals rarely require blood. There are also one or two powers that let you get around using your blood pool, though I can't remember where they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>And not all Magic requires Quint. My point is less if the cost is always there and more that it makes some thematic sense for Blood Magic (or maybe better, Vampire Magic) to be a distinct phenomena from regular mortal Magic. Which is already what the setting says anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-19T09:46:55-07:00","id":1487023,"title":"","content":"I generally like the wide spread of Blood Magic as it provides a good way to add some flavor to Clans and individual Vampires. My main quibble with it is that, for the most part, Paths tend to fall into one of two categories: highly Clan specific powers that would probably have worked better as alternative levels of signature Disciplines, or Sorcery that aside from the power level is not really anything specifically 'cainite' and might just as well be listed in Sorcerer Revised.<br /> <br /> In retrospect, a larger pool of Paths with different cultural flavors in a general supplement like 1e Sorcerer, with a unified system would probably have worked better for Revised than the patchwork approach. Dunno, maybe 5e is going to do that with Blood Sorcery and Sorcerer 5e, but I doubt it. But I like Blood Sorcery as a decidedly different thing than mortal Sorcery.<br /> <br /> As for the Tremere, they are still the only Clan that is purposefully built around magick. They are Clan <i>and House </i>Tremere. Magick Inc. I can't see any other Clans threaten that position any time soon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":27477,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","user":"voidshaper","date":". 07-19-2022, 12:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-19T10:36:09-07:00","id":1487025,"title":"","content":"Personally, I like to run Thaumaturgy and necromancy as something that's relatively easy to buy into but something that becomes very expensive to progress in if you're not blessed with being one of the magic master races. Knowledge for the first two levels can be bought from Nosferatu, Malkavians, Anarchs, Settites, underperforming Tremere, the internet... It'll cost a lot, you'll generally waste a lot of time, but it's great business for the seller. Once you've chosen your style, it's difficult to change, and thaumaturgy is limited by knowledge, so whoever sold you Thaumaturgy 1 is probably going to be the person selling you Thaumaturgy 2 and so on. In most disciplines, the first dot is most useful, but this isn't true for Thaumaturgy and to some degree necromancy; the first dot is a taster (though it requires significantly more investment than the second and so this isn't like drugs where you can give away a freebie).<br /> <br /> Learning thaumaturgy will get your average vampire into a good amount of debt, and the more lucrative abilities are hoarded or sold at exorbitant prices. So although access is widespread, few people actually bother much, other disciplines come with no strings attached after all. A cheaper method would be to join a cult. But then you're in a cult.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 07-19-2022, 01:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-19T11:16:01-07:00","id":1487028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486804-blood-magic-at-this-point-is-extremely-common?p=1487025#post1487025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> A cheaper method would be to join a cult. But then you're in a cult.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see absolutely nothing wrong with this. Plus, the Sects are technically cults. The Sabbat however, is the most cultish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-19T12:21:38-07:00","id":1487039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486804-blood-magic-at-this-point-is-extremely-common?p=1486907#post1486907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my opinion, vampires should have SOMETHING that allows them to duplicate classic Dracula powers like weather-control, making doors open and close, and making all the candles in a room light or snuff. However, I really don't care how that is achieved.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's my preference too. You want to be able to emulate certain tropes. Which is why I made certain Thaumaturgical Paths like Movement of Mind, Lure of Flames, and Weather Control knowledge that pre-dated the Tremere, and is known to the general vampire population. This doesn't mean such knowledge is common - in the sense that any jack vampire knows how to do it. Just that there are vampires who know it regardless of clan, sect, or any other faction. It's just finding the mentors who can show you such &quot;tricks&quot;.<br /> <br /> The idea that this knowledge was gained through something like the Scholomance, rather than a &quot;natural&quot; power of vampires, is fine by me.<br /> <br /> You only need 1 dot in Lure of Flames and Movement of Mind to do what is above. And that's the limit of most practitioners. A few get to rank 3 in Movement of Mind so they can fly. If it's in the Lost Boys, I want even Anarchs to have the chance to learn how to do it. David learning it from a mentor who then taught his own crew is OK as the little secret of their Anarch gang. Weather Control is limited to actual scholars of the Occult, but there are a fair number of those.<br /> <br /> Outside of this general knowledge pool, most other Paths are limited to specific factions, and the Tremere have a lot of exclusive knowledge.<br /> <br /> I would not say Blood Magic is common, meaning it's available to most characters. It's just ubiquitous in the sense that such (general) knowledge is spread around and available. But learning such occult mastery is hard. It's more of an art than a science. And it is not something commonly taught, or has manuals that show you how to do it. Most characters have no aptitude for it. And many who might would rather spend their time on other things. I want to keep it relatively rare in the setting. Every ST will find a different balance they like for their games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-19T12:28:19-07:00","id":1487040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486804-blood-magic-at-this-point-is-extremely-common?p=1487028#post1487028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I see absolutely nothing wrong with this. Plus, the Sects are technically cults. The Sabbat however, is the most cultish.</div> </div> </div> </div>While the Camarilla has a few cult-hallmarks it's really just politics. Beyond that, the cults we know in the WoD that probably teach magic are pretty... eh. <br /> <br /> Top Tier:<br /> FoS: wash your hands with piss, some really nasty hazing to get in, other than that it's sex, drugs, egyptology and rock'n roll. <br /> Your sire is a new age sorcerer: The cool aid ritual can't be done on you, there are few cons to this kind of cult, unless of course you start believing you're ready to be baptized by the sun of course. <br /> <br /> Mid:<br /> Gehenna cults- you will get killed if caught. But I suppose half the cities elders are going to be here so it'll be a good way to make connections. <br /> Assamites- Delusional badass. <br /> Inconnu- How did you get here? <br /> CoOsiris- Gaining power and being humane, no sir, I don't see a paradox here. <br /> Giovanni- Tying yourself to this family is a good way to make sure your great grandson takes after you. I don't see the appeal of corpses, but I'll do it if you offer enough money. <br /> <br /> Shit:<br /> Baharri- I don't care for that level of pain. <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Infernal thrall- Nope. </span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://